(730621, 76540, 6388, '<td valign="top">couldn''t you have found a prettier model?  Nice pic despite the subject. might have burned the windows a bit, plus the glow off GKs forehead.  a little more contrast would be nice, but that''s just my preference.<br/>on another note...isn''t he the cetre of attention enough? :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-24 10:52:47.</i></td>', 'couldn''t you have found a prettier model?  Nice pic despite the subject. might have burned the windows a bit, plus the glow off GKs forehead.  a little more contrast would be nice, but that''s just my preference.on another note...isn''t he the cetre of attention enough? :)', '2004-05-21 17:29:40.000000', '2004-05-24 11:52:47.000000', 1),
(730623, 77102, 6388, '<td valign="top">very nice.  this is one of those pics that I''d like better off-centre (I''m sure you took those too), but given the challenge is perfectly suitable.  the glow through the clouds is phenomenal.  I might have opted for a little more sky and a little less earth, but that one of those things that we leave to the anal voters and their need to analyze the ''dead centre'' semantic to death :).  great job in either case (looking forward to outtakes).<br/>Pedro</td>', 'very nice.  this is one of those pics that I''d like better off-centre (I''m sure you took those too), but given the challenge is perfectly suitable.  the glow through the clouds is phenomenal.  I might have opted for a little more sky and a little less earth, but that one of those things that we leave to the anal voters and their need to analyze the ''dead centre'' semantic to death :).  great job in either case (looking forward to outtakes).Pedro', '2004-05-21 17:33:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(730626, 76347, 6388, '<td valign="top">great shot, not so great colour to put Puggsly on :)  something a little more contrasty would help define him in the centre a little better i think.  the focus in nice and sharp, and his expression is priceless (or perhaps ''her'' I can''t tell from this angle - we''ll leave that one of ''unusual perspectives'' :))<br/>Pedro</td>', 'great shot, not so great colour to put Puggsly on :)  something a little more contrasty would help define him in the centre a little better i think.  the focus in nice and sharp, and his expression is priceless (or perhaps ''her'' I can''t tell from this angle - we''ll leave that one of ''unusual perspectives'' :))Pedro', '2004-05-21 17:34:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(730629, 76805, 6388, '<td valign="top">cool. not sure how well it will do in this challenge, but makes a very nice photo nonetheless.  If this were mine, I''d try burning those mountains in the background right down to shadows which would really punctuate the field and separate the sky.<br/>good luck,<br/>Pedro</td>', 'cool. not sure how well it will do in this challenge, but makes a very nice photo nonetheless.  If this were mine, I''d try burning those mountains in the background right down to shadows which would really punctuate the field and separate the sky.good luck,Pedro', '2004-05-21 17:36:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(730633, 76597, 6388, '<td valign="top">the colour and lighting are a little flat.  bump your contrast and it should really help sharpen it up (it''s hard to tell how sharp it really is due to the lack of contrating edges in my opinion).  A little dodging and burning would go a long way here i think.  nice shot.<br/>Pedro</td>', 'the colour and lighting are a little flat.  bump your contrast and it should really help sharpen it up (it''s hard to tell how sharp it really is due to the lack of contrating edges in my opinion).  A little dodging and burning would go a long way here i think.  nice shot.Pedro', '2004-05-21 17:38:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(730635, 77137, 6388, '<td valign="top">very well done.  aquariums are notoriously hard to shoot well, so you''ve done a great job with this.  Very nice clarity and sharpness.  a little more contrast wouldn''t hurt, but it''s nice as it is.  I''ll be looking to see what lens you shot this with.  <br/>Pedro</td>', 'very well done.  aquariums are notoriously hard to shoot well, so you''ve done a great job with this.  Very nice clarity and sharpness.  a little more contrast wouldn''t hurt, but it''s nice as it is.  I''ll be looking to see what lens you shot this with.  Pedro', '2004-05-21 17:39:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(730639, 76856, 6388, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting and focus except for the blown out part of the stem.  i''d burn that down a little to even it out.  the shallow depth seems to work nicely.  The purple glow makes it look like Moodville''s shot of a few weeks ago, but that''s neither here no there - a compliment, really :)<br/> <br/>Pedro</td>', 'I like the lighting and focus except for the blown out part of the stem.  i''d burn that down a little to even it out.  the shallow depth seems to work nicely.  The purple glow makes it look like Moodville''s shot of a few weeks ago, but that''s neither here no there - a compliment, really :) Pedro', '2004-05-21 17:41:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(730650, 76685, 6388, '<td valign="top">a little fill-flash would hav both scared the heck out of this guy, and brightened him up.  tough call.  A little dodging and burning would help increase the contrast and bring out some features.  great focus and sharpness.  well done.<br/> <br/>Pedro</td>', 'a little fill-flash would hav both scared the heck out of this guy, and brightened him up.  tough call.  A little dodging and burning would help increase the contrast and bring out some features.  great focus and sharpness.  well done. Pedro', '2004-05-21 17:57:24.000000', NULL, 1),
