(734467, 77060, 20774, '<td valign="top">This is a really wonderful photo, i really like the color of the eyes they really stick out! It is really well composed! At once more REALLY good good picture! REALLY :)</td>', 'This is a really wonderful photo, i really like the color of the eyes they really stick out! It is really well composed! At once more REALLY good good picture! REALLY :)', '2004-05-24 23:34:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(734517, 77060, 8891, '<td valign="top">Great one, Kosta! Very striking image and wow! Those eyes!</td>', 'Great one, Kosta! Very striking image and wow! Those eyes!', '2004-05-25 00:15:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(734520, 76966, 4493, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/> <br/>While I find the overall shot nice and the feeling of a snowflake comes across, I think that the uneven lighting and ''shadow'' area in the center distract from the overall pleasing mood this image should have. I like your contrast and composition and the greens are nice and subtle. Your sharpening may be just a bit much by looking at the edge of the petals.<br/> <br/>Overall nice capture... the bug is a nice touch too :-)<br/> <br/>-danny</td>', 'Critique Club: While I find the overall shot nice and the feeling of a snowflake comes across, I think that the uneven lighting and ''shadow'' area in the center distract from the overall pleasing mood this image should have. I like your contrast and composition and the greens are nice and subtle. Your sharpening may be just a bit much by looking at the edge of the petals. Overall nice capture... the bug is a nice touch too :-) -danny', '2004-05-25 00:16:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(734528, 76259, 22022, '<td valign="top">Very creative... Great ilumination and very detailed image... I liked the frogs face, it''s very funny.. Congratulations.</td>', 'Very creative... Great ilumination and very detailed image... I liked the frogs face, it''s very funny.. Congratulations.', '2004-05-25 00:21:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(734529, 76144, 4493, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Nice to see you take a different approach to a standard rose shot. I think that for DPC this image may be more than the average voter can appreciate. For me, I like the gradient you''ve used. I do think that if the overall exposure of the rose had been better, you''d have achieved an even better result. You can see in the highlight areas of the petals that you have large ''flat'' areas of color. These areas would prolly be overexposed areas that didn''t take your color treatment well. The focus may be somewhat soft as well. Not sure if that was your intent, but it keeps the image from having a professional polish. <br/> <br/>Overall I think this was a nice change of pace. A few tweaks and you''d have a very interesting print to hang on your wall.<br/> <br/>-danny</td>', 'Critique Club: Nice to see you take a different approach to a standard rose shot. I think that for DPC this image may be more than the average voter can appreciate. For me, I like the gradient you''ve used. I do think that if the overall exposure of the rose had been better, you''d have achieved an even better result. You can see in the highlight areas of the petals that you have large ''flat'' areas of color. These areas would prolly be overexposed areas that didn''t take your color treatment well. The focus may be somewhat soft as well. Not sure if that was your intent, but it keeps the image from having a professional polish.  Overall I think this was a nice change of pace. A few tweaks and you''d have a very interesting print to hang on your wall. -danny', '2004-05-25 00:21:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(734536, 76726, 4493, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Greetings,<br/> <br/>Not a whole lot of in depth critiquing I can do on this shot. The overall lighting is good (thanks sun), the sharpness is very good as well as the exposure. Not many cameras have too much difficulty with bright daylight. The composition is fine and your subject is centered, but the tail and string are both pulling my eye away from the main subject of your shot. This leads me to think that a different crop would make this a stronger shot, but would have lost your ''centered'' composition. <br/> <br/>The clouds and streamers are very playful and colors are strong, the composition is the weak part of this shot but was needed for this challenge.<br/> <br/>-danny</td>', 'Critique Club: Greetings, Not a whole lot of in depth critiquing I can do on this shot. The overall lighting is good (thanks sun), the sharpness is very good as well as the exposure. Not many cameras have too much difficulty with bright daylight. The composition is fine and your subject is centered, but the tail and string are both pulling my eye away from the main subject of your shot. This leads me to think that a different crop would make this a stronger shot, but would have lost your ''centered'' composition.  The clouds and streamers are very playful and colors are strong, the composition is the weak part of this shot but was needed for this challenge. -danny', '2004-05-25 00:26:23.000000', NULL, 0),
